Enhancement: Verify uploaded packs exist before writing the index

Restic now checks that every pack file uploaded by the current backup still
exists in the backend before flushing the index. If a pack vanished after the
upload, for example due to a faulty or misconfigured backend, the backup is
aborted with an error instead of writing an index that references
non-existent packs. The index and the snapshot are then not modified, so the
repository stays consistent and the backup can be retried.

The check only uses metadata lookups for packs uploaded by the current
repository instance, so it adds no significant overhead and does not affect
backups running concurrently against the same repository. Packs left behind by
an aborted backup can be reindexed with `restic repair index`; damaged packs
continue to be detected by `restic check` and repaired with
`restic repair packs`.
